<p>NOTES: Full co name is Mallinckrodt Inc.  </p>
<p>Net EPS for 4 qtrs of FY96 more than full year per shr results by $0.01 from decrease in shrs outstanding.</p>
<p>(1) 1997 continuing oper earnings included Q1 one-time R&amp;D charge of $6.0 million, $3.8 million after taxes, or $0.05/shr from alliance to develop magnetic resonance imaging technology.</p>
<p>On March 31, 1997, co disposed of Fries &amp; Fries Inc, a wholly owned subsidiary which owned co's 50-percent interest in Tastemaker, a flavor joint venture with Hercules Inc. Co recorded net after-tax gain of $270.6 million on disposal, which included in discontinued operations.</p>
<p>On May 15, 1997, co approved formal plan to divest animal health segment. Co included estimated after-tax loss on disposal of $275.3 million in discontinued operations for Q3.</p>
<p>Prior period results of Fries &amp; Fries Inc and animal health reclassified to discontinued operations.</p>
<p>(2) Divested operations relates primarily to the divested cosmetic, electronic chemicals businesses.</p>
<p>(3) During Q2 1996, animal feed ingredients business sold. Results for feed ingredients business accounted for as discontinued operation, and prior period results restated.</p>
<p>Other principal factors affecting discontinued operations were after-tax gain of $35.4 million on sale of feed ingredients business and after-tax provision for environmental costs of $15.6 million. Results for 1994, 1993, 1992 restated, as well.</p>
